---
// ── Why pichi ─────────────────────────────────────────
---

<section class="section">
  <div class="section-title">Why pichi</div>
  <div class="props">
    <div class="prop">
      <h3>Run anywhere</h3>
      <p>One image runs on Linux, macOS, and Windows hosts, and on bare metal — no rebuild.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prop">
      <h3>Real isolation</h3>
      <p>Your own kernel and memory, not a slice of the host's.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prop">
      <h3>Verifiable boot</h3>
      <p>
        A small boot chain with a deterministic launch measurement, so you can check what actually
        booted.<span class="note"
          >Hardware attestation targets confidential-computing platforms (AMD SEV-SNP, with Intel
          TDX and Arm CCA drafted) — on the roadmap, not yet shipping.</span
        >
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="prop">
      <h3>Container-like workflow</h3>
      <p>Pull, push, run, and cache over any OCI registry — the workflow you already know.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .props {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .prop {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.35rem 1.5rem;
  }
  .prop h3 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: #fff;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  .prop p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .prop .note {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    opacity: 0.85;
  }
</style>
